00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.489
With that out the way, thank you for playing,
now let's get into Season 1 of Squid Game.

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:49.649
Ok so Squid Game follows Gi-Hun a man who's
down on his luck after losing just about everything

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.460
that means something to him.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:55.940
His marriage failed, he lost his job, is in
deep over his head with gangsters and now

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.899
faces the fact that his daughter is going
to be leaving South Korea with her mother

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:01.109
and new family.

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:06.230
To make matters worse his mother is also at
deaths door and she requires medical treatment

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.100
in order to save his life.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.280
Seems like things are going worse than this
channel is however his fortune seemingly changes

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.670
when he meets a man at a train station that
offers him the opportunity of a life and death

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.670
time.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.229
Desperate for money Gi-Hun finds himself somewhat
squidnapped and drafted into a battle royale

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:36.250
between himself and 456 contestants worth
a grand prize of 45.6 billion.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.439
Throughout we watch as the players are wittled
down to one in games of red and green, honey

00:01:40.439 --> 00:01:45.329
combs, tug of war, hopscotch and one that
will have you losing your marbles due to the

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:46.329
betrayals in it.

00:01:46.329 --> 00:01:51.590
The season is a blast to watch and early on
it sets up this idea of division within colours

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.550
that thematically ends up coming full circle
by the end.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:58.430
The colours Red and Green are introduced and
these are actually classed as opposites on

00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.899
the colour spectrum.

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:03.719
Both are mentioned in the passwords, they
become the name of the first game and even

00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:07.100
the contestants wear green whilst the guards
don red.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.430
The show is absolutely laced with these opposing
colours and they in many ways very much represent

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:15.070
the divide between the powerful and powerless.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.519
As we know from our own society this divide
is often showcased between the rich and the

00:02:19.519 --> 00:02:23.680
poor and we learn that there are a vast number
of wealthy men who actually oversee the entire

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.260
operation and that this is all for their entertainment.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.980
Rather than being seen as people, the players
are very much just numbers and this is demonstrated

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.150
in the fact that they are literally given
these as their names.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:39.480
Along the way, Gi-Hun meets an elderly man
named number 1 and the fact that he's the

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.070
first drafted into the game should give you
a clue towards his true identity at the end.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:47.930
Gi-Hun is the last number in the game and
throughout the season we watch as he very

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.180
much works his way to 1.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:54.720
At one point number 1 even ends the game and
gives the survivors of the first one a chance

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.269
to go off and live their lives but they all
return, desperate for the money.

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:03.520
In the end all that remains are Gi-Hun and
Sang-woo, two childhood friends who led very

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:08.349
different lives but both found themselves
in the same spot come the end of the game.

00:03:08.349 --> 00:03:12.379
The final competition is the titular Squid
Game and we watch as the game they played

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:15.189
as children decides who will live and die.

00:03:15.189 --> 00:03:19.430
It's an awesome final battle and they even
bring some rain in in order to add some dramatics

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:20.670
to the final showdown.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:25.750
Gi-Hun bests Sang-Woo but rather than killing
him he brings up the clause that if both players

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:30.439
forfeit then the game will be null and void
and thus they'll both get to go home.

00:03:30.439 --> 00:03:34.489
This will be with nothing but Gi-Hun would
rather put a stop to the death than gain the

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:39.519
money but rather than forfeiting Sang-Woo
ends his own life because of what he's done

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.650
in the game.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:45.170
All he does is make Gi-Hun promise that he'll
look after his mother and then he stabs himself

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.409
leaving Gi-Hun as the last man standing.

00:03:47.409 --> 00:03:52.659
Now whilst this game is going on we see a
police officer who's brother disappeared investigating

00:03:52.659 --> 00:03:55.379
to island in an attempt to learn of his fate.

00:03:55.379 --> 00:03:59.540
Throughout he sees things from the other side
but a big twist comes towards the end when

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:03.719
we learn that his sibling is actually a character
known as the Front Man who is running the

00:04:03.719 --> 00:04:04.719
operation.

00:04:04.719 --> 00:04:09.020
He attempts to alert the police to the whereabouts
of the island as well as what's going on but

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.120
the fact that the game is still continuing
at the end lets us know that the operation

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.120
wasn't shut down.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:19.130
Now one of the big questions surrounding the
series is whether he survived or not.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.530
Towards the end of the season he's shot and
though the character takes a tumble off a

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:27.470
cliff into the ocean, we never actually see
a body and therefore can assume that he's

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.610
still alive.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:33.330
Hwang Jun-Ho is only shot in the shoulder,
much like his brother and with the Front Man

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.120
not dying from the wound it is likely that
his brother didn't either.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.680
However we do know that he didn't shut down
the Squid Games so it'll be interesting to

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.650
see how he's brought back in future seasons.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:49.000
After the prize money is given to Gi-Hun he
returns home but open getting there he finds

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.389
that his mother has died.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:55.500
Due to him participating in the games he wasn't
there for her in her final few days and it's

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.221
a devastating ending that feels like a real
gut punch on what was already an extremly

00:05:00.221 --> 00:05:01.740
brutal series.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:05.310
It's at this point that we pick up one year
later and discover that Gi-Hun is still living

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.940
life in the exact same manner that he was
before he won.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.910
The money that he saught after for so long
was actually worth nothing to him in the end

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.290
and the real people who meant something to
him were lost whilst he tried to seek out

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.540
these riches.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:21.200
It's very much a case of the only thing worse
than not getting what you want is getting

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.570
it and he's trapped in a state of grief by
himself with life having lost it's meaning.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:29.500
At this point he's given a card which is similar
to the one that started everything off and

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.640
on the back of it he finds an address which
leads him to an apartment.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.669
Here he finds Number 1 bed bound and we learn
that he was actually behind the entire game.

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:41.880
Much like Gi-Hun, possessing all that money
ended up meaning very little to him and in

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:46.330
his boredom he created the games in order
to entertain himself and his rich friends.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:50.500
He lived life believing that people wouldn't
help one another and uses a drunk man across

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.740
the street as confirmation of this.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.520
In his last few moments he plays one final
game in which the pair bet whether anyone

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:02.040
will stop to help him and because of their
choices we see the cynicism within Number

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.040
1.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:08.009
Number 1 or rather Il-Nam only believed in
the worst of humanity and his entire life

00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:13.570
led him to believe that people were all self
centred only interested in...well their own

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:14.570
interests.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:18.410
However as he dies we see that people actually
arrive in order to help the man across the

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:22.190
street and it's very much an FU to him in
his final moments.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.320
Now we never learn whether Il-Nam as he's
called sees this but in all honesty it doesn't

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.419
really matter.

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:31.740
His entire life ended up becoming dedicated
to the idea that he didn't need to help others

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:35.819
because other people in his position would
also be just as selfish.

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:39.949
Il-Nam could've shared his wealth with anyone
at any time but he believed deep down that

00:06:39.949 --> 00:06:44.110
people were all as bad as each other and that
if they were where he was that they wouldn't

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:45.349
help him either.

00:06:45.349 --> 00:06:49.650
This was somewhat shown in the game of marbles
in which Gi-Hun lied and cheated in order

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:50.930
to get ahead.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:54.509
Though we will never know whether he he knew
of the homeless man's fate or not it really

00:06:54.509 --> 00:06:59.190
doesn't matter as this moment inspires Gi-Hun
to do something with the money rather than

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.660
letting it go to waste.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:05.039
Gi-Hun gets a hair cut and has it dyed red
showing that he is somewhat the one that is

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:06.870
in the position of power now.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:11.370
Rather than being a malevolent d**khead like
the rest of the reds though he takes a player's

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:15.940
brother out of an orphanage that she wanted
to rescue him from and places him in Sang-Woo's

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:18.170
care who he makes extremely rich.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:22.620
He lives up to his two promises and though
it seems like a happy ending it's all quickly

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.759
cut short when we realise that the game is
still going.

00:07:25.759 --> 00:07:29.940
Though Il-Nam died the game didn't die with
him and at a train station he comes across

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.810
the man who recruited him played by Gong Yoo.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:36.770
You might recognise him from the seminal horror
movie Train To Busan and I believe that come

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:39.580
the second season that he will play a much
bigger role.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:44.180
He is clearly still tied into the operation
and Gi-Hun takes the card from the person

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.490
he was attempting to rope into the game.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:51.080
The season closes out with Gi-Hun about to
board a plane to LA in order to see his daugther

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.110
but after calling the number on the card he
comes to the conclusion that the game is going

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:58.930
to continue and that hundreds more people
will die if he doesn't step in and do something

00:07:58.930 --> 00:07:59.960
about it.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:03.990
He tells the Front Man that he's coming for
them and this of course carries a lot of weight

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.440
for Season 2.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.200
Now I believe that Gi-Hun will meet up with
Hwang Jun-Ho and that together the pair will

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.210
end up going to the island in order to stop
the games.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:17.280
Gi-Hun was gassed during transport so he doesn't
know how to get there, however Hwang Jun-Ho

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.650
does if he made it out and managed to swim
back to the mainland.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:25.190
With Gi-Huns resources and new found life
he'll be able to equip Hwang Jun-Ho with the

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.940
necessary means to take down the Squid Game
Gang.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:33.280
This is obviously a big twist as one of the
lessons he learned in his mothers death was

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.690
not to abandon those that he loved but he's
very much abandoning hundreds of people to

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:40.150
their deaths if he decides to travel to LA.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:44.010
He's damned if he does and damned if he doesn't
and I see this more as an ending in which

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:47.630
he's sacrificing his own happiness in order
to help others.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.890
Again this is something that Il-Nam would
never do and thus it's a great signal of the

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.140
character coming full circle.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:57.650
Now there are other potentials for season
2 and we do know that the games have been

00:08:57.650 --> 00:08:59.300
going on for decades.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:03.420
There's evidence they even existed in the
80s and it would be interesting to explore

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.550
not only their origins but also Il-Nams who
of course founded them.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:10.850
There's also the fact that we know these are
being run internationally and though it's

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:16.490
a long shot I'd love to see Netflix also bring
in the european and western games as series

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:20.770
to show us what was happening there before
we build to an overarching narrative involving

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:21.770
all the winners.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:26.770
Either way there's a lot of potential directions
they could take it and I have to say I absolutely

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.420
loved this season and can't wait to see more.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:33.710
It was absolutely gripping not knowing who
would live and die and it made for a season

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:38.080
that I happily binged in one day just to see
what the outcome would be.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:42.030
This is a great character study that really
gets to the meat of what it means to survive

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:47.110
when it costs others so much and I think the
show handled a lot of it's elements in spectacular

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.160
fashion.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:52.050
Whenever a Korean show comes out on Netflix
I always try and cover it as they're pretty

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:56.040
much brilliant across the board and this is
no different.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:10:00.150
Squid Game pulled me right in and it gets
a...

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:01.430
9.5/10

